✅ Experiment 3: Site-to-Site VPN in Cisco Packet Tracer

Tools: Cisco Packet Tracer

Step-by-Step:

1. Drag and drop:

2 Routers (e.g., 2911)

2 Switches

2 PCs



2. Configure IPs:

PC-A: 192.168.1.2/24

PC-B: 192.168.2.2/24

Routers LAN & WAN accordingly



3. Enable IKE and IPsec: On both routers (CLI):

crypto isakmp policy 1
encr aes
hash sha
authentication pre-share
group 5
lifetime 86400

crypto isakmp key 123456 address <peer-ip>
crypto ipsec transform-set MYSET esp-aes esp-sha-hmac
crypto map MYMAP 10 ipsec-isakmp
set peer <peer-ip>
set transform-set MYSET
match address 101

access-list 101 permit ip 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255 192.168.2.0 0.0.0.255
interface s0/0/0
crypto map MYMAP


4. Test VPN:

Ping from PC-A to PC-B

Use simulation mode to observe VPN packets





